Lambda expressions provide a concise way to represent functional interfaces using anonymous functions.

Example:
interface MyInterface {
 void show();
}
class Demo {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 MyInterface m = () -> System.out.println("Hello Lambda");
 m.show();
 }
}

Lambda expressions reduce boilerplate code and improve readability.

The Streams API is used to process collections of data in a functional style. It supports operations like filter, map, and forEach.

Example:
import java.util.*;
class StreamDemo {
 public static void main(String[] args) {
 List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3, 4);
 list.stream().filter(n -> n % 2 == 0).forEach(System.out::println);
 }
}

Streams do not modify the original collection.

Streams API Java मध्ये collections process करण्यासाठी functional style देते. यात filter, map, forEach सारखे operations असतात.

Example:
List<Integer> list = Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3, 4);
list.stream().filter(n -> n % 2 == 0).forEach(System.out::println);

Streams मुळे original collection modify होत नाही।

